      "hints": [
        "Substitute $\\tan x = \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x} = \\frac{a + b}{a - b} = 2$.",
        "Cross-multiply to express $a$ in terms of $b$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Express $\\tan x$ as the quotient of sine and cosine:\n$$\\tan x = \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x} = \\frac{a + b}{a - b} = 2$$",
        "Cross-multiply and isolate $a$ in terms of $b$:\n$$a + b = 2(a - b) = 2a - 2b \\implies 2a - a = b + 2b \\implies a = 3b$$"
      ],
